{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/217228-rite-of-initiation","id":217228,"title":"Rite of Initiation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-02T23:37:14-07:00","id":217228,"title":"Rite of Initiation","content":"So in our Sweden <b>Werewolf</b> game, my players end Ordeals from Firstborns. They should be initiated to Tribes now, but they are only Forsaken in region. They mentor is ex-Bale Hound, and don't know proper rituals, as she was introduced to sect from beginning.<br /> <br /> So how should mix Tribes pact resolve? I got idea of one ceremony, on what pack's Itheaur marks every member with his Tribe glyps in hunt's blood. But it's only rought idea. What Auspices would be best for this kind of things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T10:11:04-07:00","id":217490,"title":"","content":"Not one to tell you how to run your game, but perhaps you should have them split to the most local regional pack of said tribes and undertake solo rites of passage. That way its personal for the characters instead of &quot;welcome to (put tribe name here)&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T14:01:05-07:00","id":217577,"title":"","content":"Have tribal spirits (not necessarily the Firstborns themselves) initiate each. Alternatively, given how the setting is... have them stick to being Ghost Wolves. Make it a feature; not a bug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T14:39:03-07:00","id":217586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/217228-rite-of-initiation?p=217490#post217490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not one to tell you how to run your game, but perhaps you should have them split to the most local regional pack of said tribes and undertake solo rites of passage. That way its personal for the characters instead of &quot;welcome to (put tribe name here)&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There aren't &quot;most local regional pack&quot;. They are shut from outside world, and they are alone, facing Bale Hounds pack. It's main premise of the game at hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternatively, given how the setting is... have them stick to being Ghost Wolves. Make it a feature; not a bug. </div> </div> </div>Being Ghost Wolves means no Gifts, and at least half of Pack is interested in them.<br /> <br /> Also, Tribes were decide weeks ago ( by players), I only need the details of intiation rite and when to perform it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T15:42:34-07:00","id":217613,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You could have them hunt down spirits, turn it into a story in and of itself; exploring through the Hisil and taking on a dangerous journey reflecting the various &quot;First&quot; ways that each tribe came into being. Reflect each tribe that the PCs want to become as a segment of the story until the finale of that chapter has the Ithaeur howling the past tribe name out for the Bale Hounds to tremble at.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This would involve the different auspices as well. The Rahu would obviously be the one to throw down challenges, the Cahalith explores what little history they can find to put the clues together, the Irraka sneaks through the darker sections of the Shadow to bring back the appropriate offerings, the Elodath negotiates, and the Ithaeur creates/performs the actual rituals for the initiation.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The big thing would be to make it personalized for that pack in particular because there are no other Forsaken around. If it\u2019s powerful enough, there could be new stories formed from what the Pack accomplished in a place that seemingly was abandoned by the People.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T08:07:25-07:00","id":218176,"title":"","content":"Being ghost wolves does not mean no gifts. It just shuts them out from specific gift lists. I dig the ghost wolf suggestion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T12:23:34-07:00","id":218402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/217228-rite-of-initiation?p=218176#post218176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being ghost wolves does not mean no gifts. It just shuts them out from specific gift lists. I dig the ghost wolf suggestion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The ghost wolf suggestion, while neat, only works if the Players want to go that route. It seems they do not, and wyrdhamster seems keen on the tribes returning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T16:00:42-07:00","id":218588,"title":"","content":"Fair point . Could have a lodge nearby, watching the area. Multi tribal","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T16:04:56-07:00","id":218593,"title":"","content":"That's the issue with settings. You have to write them in a way that facilitate things for yourself and the players. Not the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T08:31:39-07:00","id":219112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/217228-rite-of-initiation?p=218176#post218176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being ghost wolves does not mean no gifts. It just shuts them out from specific gift lists. I dig the ghost wolf suggestion.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are not shut out from any gift lists as a Ghost Wolf save the non-affinity Auspice Lists, and since they do still have auspices they have an affinity for their Auspice Lists... All other lists are just not affinity for you, which is not the same thing as NO gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T08:32:01-07:00","id":220240,"title":"","content":"A few of ideas:<br /> <br /> Early on, I wasn't too keen on the Father Wolf/Mother Luna idea, so I decided to make the Tribal Totems be more &quot;paws on&quot; and pick their members. usually thru a quick trial with them personally. The only one I got to use was Black Wolf guiding the cub thru his territory for a night dealing with the problems they found. As has already been suggested above, they don't need to be the Tribal Totems themselves, just a select rep (Crash Before The Storm versus All Father Thunder himself showing up). You could play up the isolation more by having the selected representative need time to carry news of their Oaths back to the Tribal Totems before they get access to those Gift lists. These spirits could become messengers/mentors in an on-going capacity.<br /> <br /> The Ghost Wolves is not a bad idea and would be appropriate as they don't have anyone from the Tribes to connect with. If they are interested in a particular Tribe, they can always take an Oath for that without it being specifically to the Totem in question. It shouldn't be identical to the Tribal Oath, of course, because who would have been around to tell it to them, but it can be something similar.<br /> <br /> If all they're interested in is making sure they have access to all the Gifts, just use the Spirit Perdition rules from Forsaken Chronicler's Guide. Just in case someone doesn't have this document, first of all: <b>SHAME ON YOU! GO GET IT! NOW!!! </b>Second, short version: the Spirit Perdition allows Uratha to hunt down spirits and devour them to get the Gifts they want without having to bargain for them or wait for someone to teach it to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T09:59:47-07:00","id":220304,"title":"","content":"What's wrong with bargaining? Why you got to eat them? That is so very rude!! Poor Spirits.<br /> That said... Spirit Predation is pretty cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T10:10:39-07:00","id":220313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/217228-rite-of-initiation?p=220304#post220304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's wrong with bargaining? Why you got to eat them? That is so very rude!! Poor Spirits.<br /> That said... Spirit Predation is pretty cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because they're just measly little spirits against<b> the might of the Uratha!!!!!!!! Run <i>now </i>and be EATEN, or stand your ground and be EATEN <i>SOONER</i>!!!!</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry, had to get that out of my system. It's less than a week until the full moon, so my inner Cahalith needed to get out a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 02-09-2015, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"